IMPORT prelude

-- Service Lands Act 1963 (Singapore) -- the land to which the ejectment procedure applies (s 2(1)), who may lay the information and
-- when a Magistrate's Court may summon and summarily hear the occupier (s 2(2)), the Court's duty to issue a warrant of
-- dispossession once satisfied, what the police take possession of on the Federal Lands Commissioner's behalf, and which police
-- officer may execute the warrant (s 2(3)).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/SLA1963.txt. The deposit says it "incorporates all
-- amendments up to and including 1 December 2021 and comes into operation on 31 December 2021". It carries no amendment
-- annotations; its Legislative History lists M. Act 35 of 1963 (commencement 1 November 1963) and the 1970, 1985 and 2013 Revised
-- Editions, the last in operation 31 August 2013. The deposit's metadata calls it the current version as at 1 October 2026. The
-- Arrangement of Sections is column-shifted in the deposit (the numbers 1 and 2 sit above both headings); the body has s 1 (short
-- title) and s 2 (removal of unlawful occupants), and this file follows the body.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0154 in subjects/sg/requirements.jsonl: tier 2 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by
-- everyday-life relevance. The requirement asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has asked
-- a sharper question yet. The Act has two sections, so it is encoded whole except s 1 (short title).
--
-- Not encoded: what makes an occupation "unlawful" (the Act does not say; it is left to the general law); whether any land in
-- Singapore is now "used or to be used" for Malaysian forces (a question of fact the text cannot answer); who the "Federal Lands
-- Commissioner" is today (the Act does not define the office); the procedure on a summary hearing, any appeal, any compensation for
-- crops or buildings taken, and what happens to movable property left on the land -- the Act says nothing on any of these.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Service Lands Act 1963 -- ejectment`

§§ `2(1) -- the land to which the section applies`

-- s 2(1): "The provisions of this section shall apply to lands used or to be used for the purposes of any military, naval or air
-- forces of Malaysia."
-- The text names only the forces of Malaysia. Land used by Singapore's own forces, or by any other foreign force, is not within it.
-- READING (an inference): "to be used" reaches land earmarked for those forces but not yet in use.
DECLARE Land IS ONE OF
    `land in use by the Malaysian army`
    `land in use by the Malaysian navy`
    `land in use by the Malaysian air force`
    `land set aside for future use by Malaysian forces`
    `land in use by the Singapore Armed Forces`
    `land in use by another foreign force`
    `ordinary State land`
    `private land`

GIVEN `the land` IS A Land
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 2 applies to the land` IF
    CONSIDER `the land`
    WHEN `land in use by the Malaysian army` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `land in use by the Malaysian navy` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `land in use by the Malaysian air force` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `land set aside for future use by Malaysian forces` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `2(2) -- the information, the summons and the summary hearing`

-- s 2(2): "A Magistrate's Court, on the information of the Federal Lands Commissioner or a person authorised by him that any person
-- is in unlawful occupation of any land to which this section applies, may issue a summons for the appearance before the Court of
-- the person informed against; and on his appearing to the summons or (in default of his appearance thereto) on proof of service of
-- the summons the Court may proceed in a summary way to hear and determine the information."
-- Only the Commissioner or his authorised person may inform. A landowner, another agency or a police officer acting on his own
-- account is not named. The summons is discretionary ("may").
DECLARE Informant IS ONE OF
    `the Federal Lands Commissioner`
    `a person authorised by the Federal Lands Commissioner`
    `a Singapore government land agency acting on its own account`
    `a police officer acting on his own account`
    `a private landowner`

GIVEN `the informant` IS AN Informant
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may lay the information` IF
    CONSIDER `the informant`
    WHEN `the Federal Lands Commissioner` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a person authorised by the Federal Lands Commissioner` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

DECLARE Proceeding HAS
    `the land occupied` IS A Land
    `the informant laying it` IS AN Informant
    `the information alleges unlawful occupation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the occupier appeared to the summons` IS A BOOLEAN
    `service of the summons is proved` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Court is satisfied the information is true` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the proceeding` IS A Proceeding
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Court may issue a summons` IF
        `section 2 applies to the land` (`the proceeding`'s `the land occupied`)
    AND `may lay the information` (`the proceeding`'s `the informant laying it`)
    AND `the proceeding`'s `the information alleges unlawful occupation`

-- The hearing may go ahead in the occupier's absence, but only on proof that the summons was served.
GIVEN `the proceeding` IS A Proceeding
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Court may hear and determine the information summarily` IF
        `the Court may issue a summons` `the proceeding`
    AND (    `the proceeding`'s `the occupier appeared to the summons`
         OR  `the proceeding`'s `service of the summons is proved`)

§§ `2(3) -- the warrant`

-- s 2(3): "If on the hearing of the information the Court is satisfied of the truth thereof, the Court shall by warrant require any
-- police officer specified in the warrant forthwith to dispossess and remove such person from the land, and on behalf of the Federal
-- Lands Commissioner to take possession of the land ..."
-- "shall": once satisfied, the Court has no discretion to refuse the warrant. The text gives no grace period -- "forthwith".
GIVEN `the proceeding` IS A Proceeding
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Court must issue a warrant of dispossession` IF
        `the Court may hear and determine the information summarily` `the proceeding`
    AND `the proceeding`'s `the Court is satisfied the information is true`

-- s 2(3) continued: possession of the land is taken "together with all crops growing thereon and all buildings and other immovable
-- property upon and affixed to the land".
-- READING (an inference): the words reach only growing crops and immovable property affixed to the land. Movable belongings, and
-- crops already harvested, are not named; the Act does not say what becomes of them.
DECLARE Property IS ONE OF
    `crops growing on the land`
    `a building on the land`
    `a fixed structure affixed to the land`
    `crops already harvested`
    `furniture and other movable belongings`
    `a vehicle parked on the land`

GIVEN `the property` IS A Property
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `possession is taken of it with the land` IF
    CONSIDER `the property`
    WHEN `crops growing on the land` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a building on the land` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a fixed structure affixed to the land` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- s 2(3) concluding words: "the warrant may be executed by any police officer into whose hands the warrant may come, whether or not
-- it is addressed to him."
-- Only a police officer may execute it; whether the warrant names him does not matter.
DECLARE Executor IS ONE OF
    `a police officer`
    `an officer of the Federal Lands Commissioner who is not a police officer`
    `a court bailiff`
    `a member of the armed forces`

GIVEN `the executor` IS AN Executor, `the warrant is addressed to him` IS A BOOLEAN, `the warrant has come into his hands` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may execute the warrant` IF
        `the warrant has come into his hands`
    AND CONSIDER `the executor`
        WHEN `a police officer` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE

-- For whom the land is taken: "on behalf of the Federal Lands Commissioner".
DECLARE Possessor IS ONE OF
    `the Federal Lands Commissioner`
    `the Government of Singapore`
    `the police`
    `the informant personally`

GIVEN `the possessor` IS A Possessor
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `possession is taken on behalf of` IF
    CONSIDER `the possessor`
    WHEN `the Federal Lands Commissioner` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE
